+/// The PNGs are 256 px and the marks are drawn at 16 to 30. Handing the GPU the big
+/// image and letting it pick a mip level and blend two of them gives soft, slightly
+/// smeared marks. Here the shrink is done once, on the CPU, with a Lanczos filter, and
+/// the result is cached per size.
+///
+/// Every glyph is white ink on transparent (the tint is applied when drawing), so only
+/// the alpha channel is resized and the colour is rebuilt as pure white: no dark fringe
+/// from the colour of fully transparent pixels bleeding into the edge.
